commit 6d3220afaa7958357f889e64c827ff27fa36e476

C03: installing a Python package with pip is answered by a read of whether it is installed in each registered Python (PIP1817)

New read-only operation software.python.package.status(package): the PEP 514 enumeration of software.python.status is factored out and pip show runs in every registered Python with an executable (installed, package version, pip available per Python); nothing is installed. The mind reads «instalá X con/usando pip», «pip install X», «instalá el paquete X» and «tengo X instalado en python» as that read, binds the package name, and the composer states in which Python versions the package is installed with the exact version strings.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>


